// RISE settles upward, SHIFT downward — the same reveal, mirrored, which is exactly what
// the direction vector expresses. The `takeIf` fallbacks matter: a spec carrying
// direction=DEFAULT resolves to a ZERO vector, and multiplying by it would leave the
// effect motionless. RISE historically ignored direction entirely and always rose, so UP
// is its fallback and its rendering is unchanged. (A one-shot RISE is Canva's ارتقاء and
// never reaches here — see resolveCanvaOneShotVisualState; this is the loop bob.)
LayerAnimationType.RISE,
LayerAnimationType.SHIFT -> {
    val riseY = vector.y.takeIf { it != 0f }
        ?: if (animation.type == LayerAnimationType.SHIFT) 1f else -1f
    LayerAnimationVisualState(
        translationY = -riseY * (1f - progress) * maxOf(16f, height * 0.22f) * intensity,
        alphaMultiplier = (0.12f + progress * 0.88f).coerceIn(0f, 1f)
    )
}

